# Docker build-context hygiene (DR-C1, docker-regression-reliability-plan).
#
# Every image in this repo builds with the repo root as its context
# (docker/regression/docker-compose.test.yml, docker-compose.cross-server.yml,
# docker/MJAPI). Without this file each build transferred a multi-GB context —
# .git (~1.7GB), node_modules (~2.8GB), docker/regression/test-results (~1.9GB)
# on a working checkout — and `COPY packages/` imported host build state
# (dist/, nested node_modules, tool caches) into images that run their own
# clean install + build.
#
# Rule of thumb: sources, manifests, metadata, migrations, and demo SQL go in;
# VCS history, dependencies, build outputs, caches, run artifacts, and secrets
# stay out.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded: docker/regression/.docker-generated/ — the
# container-produced codegen overlay that Dockerfile.api / Dockerfile.explorer
# explicitly COPY (see those files for why).

# ── VCS + CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github

# ── Dependencies — images run their own npm ci ─────────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules

# ── Build outputs and tool caches — host state must never leak into images ─
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.angular

# ── Regression-run artifacts (screenshots/reports; GBs, never COPY'd) ──────
docker/regression/test-results

# ── Workbench workspace bind-mount (can hold a full second MJ checkout) ────
docker/workbench/workspace

# ── Secrets / env files — never ship credentials to the build daemon ───────
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# ── Local tool state / logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.playwright-cli
**/*.log
